1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:33,079
Welcome to this complete tutorial of USBAnywhere, the free and open-source solution for sharing USB devices over your network. If you have used VirtualHere, you know that its free tier restricts you to a single simultaneous device, and its license costs forty-nine dollars per server. With USBAnywhere, you get unlimited simultaneous devices, zero licensing fees, Microsoft WHQL-certified drivers, and ultra-low latency profiles for gaming and simulation.

2
00:00:33,079 --> 00:01:00,231
Configuring the server on your Raspberry Pi or Linux board is instantaneous. From the Windows client, click the SSH button, enter your user and IP address, and click the green One-Click Auto-Setup button. Our automated script installs the background daemon and enables an intelligent udev hotplug rule that automatically shares any USB peripheral the second you plug it in, with zero manual commands.

3
00:01:00,231 --> 00:01:24,695
When launching USBAnywhere on Windows ten or eleven, the app automatically scans your local subnet, discovers active servers, and displays their exact ping in milliseconds. To connect any peripheral, simply double-click it or right-click and select Connect. You can also save devices to Favorites so they automatically reconnect whenever your computer starts.

4
00:01:24,695 --> 00:01:59,647
USBAnywhere features two dedicated reception engines within the Windows kernel. Low-Latency mode uses direct callbacks designed to eliminate input lag on Xbox and PlayStation controllers, SimRacing steering wheels, load-cell pedals, and VR trackers with full force feedback. It is the ideal companion for Moonlight, Sunshine, and Steam Deck streaming. For webcams, 3D printers, or flash drives, Zero-Copy mode provides maximum throughput without CPU overhead.

5
00:01:59,647 --> 00:02:30,543
Need to access USB peripherals away from home? The VPN dialog integrates directly with Tailscale and ZeroTier, letting you connect to remote servers over the Internet without opening router ports. USBAnywhere is available in both installer and hybrid portable packages, and installs in seconds using Winget or Scoop. Visit our official GitHub repository, download version three point zero, and leave VirtualHere paywalls behind forever.

